course: dictionary
lesson: 1936
title: Praise and commendation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A commendation is official praise. It is more than a kind word: it is praise given formally, often as a certificate or an award, for something someone did well or bravely.
explain: Context shows you this. «The old seaman's commendations made the young sailor blush for pleasure.» The words blush and pleasure tell you the commendations were something good, so commendations must mean praise. Try the swap: "the old seaman's praise" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Commendation can also mean praise in general. In church or other formal language, it can mean a prayer that places someone in God's care, especially a person who is dying. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning fits.
fact: Commendation means praise, often official praise, for doing something well or bravely.
fact: «Receive a commendation» means you are given an award or certificate for good work.
fact: «Highly commended» means praised strongly, often in a competition or contest.
fact: A commendation for bravery is given to people such as police officers and firefighters.
fact: Commendation is also a noun you can use without "a", as in "praise and commendation", when you mean praise in general.
exercise: «The old seaman's commendations made the young sailor blush for pleasure.» What does commendations mean here? | Warnings | *Praise | Gifts for a birthday | Scolding
exercise: Maya got a commendation for bravery after she helped a neighbour out of a fire. What is a commendation? | A kind of fire alarm | A type of lunch box | A formal prayer for a sick friend | *Official praise or an award for bravery
exercise: Ms Patel says, «Your story was highly commended.» What does highly commended mean? | Read out loud twice | Badly marked | *Praised strongly, often for doing very well | Put in detention
test: «Her teacher wrote a commendation on her report for kind helpfulness.» What is a commendation here? | A spelling test | A warning letter | *Praise for good work | A bill to pay
test: In church, a commendation can be a prayer for someone who is dying. Which words best describe this meaning? | A type of lamp | A school trophy | A spelling game | *A prayer that places someone in God's care
exam: Ruby's grandad received a commendation for bravery. Which word is closest in meaning to commendation? | *Praise | Question | Punishment | Argument
